        "original_id": "ea129fb9-53a4-5d6c-bc0f-9f321a7de6b0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alberic II of Spoleto, Marozia, Pope Leo VII, Luigi Calabresi\n- Places: Rome, Milan, Italy\n- Roles: ruler of Rome, Roman noblewoman, pope, police officer, Italian State Police official, King of Italy\n- Organizations: Italian State Police\nFacts:\n- Marozia, born Maria and also known as Mariuccia or Mariozza, lived from 890 to 937.\n- Marozia was a Roman noblewoman, the alleged mistress of Pope Sergius III, and was given the titles \"senatrix\" and \"patricia\" of Rome by Pope John X.\n- Alberic II of Spoleto lived from 912 to 954.\n- Alberic II of Spoleto ruled Rome from 932 to 954 after deposing his mother Marozia and his stepfather, King Hugh of Italy.\n- Pope Leo VII's election to the papacy was secured by Alberic II of Spoleto, who was the ruler of Rome at the time.\n- Luigi Calabresi was born in Rome on 14 November 1937 and died in Milan on 17 May 1972.\n- Luigi Calabresi was a police officer and an Italian State Police official in Milan, Italy.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "aa169ff5-3672-575d-b360-62e12a6d8c56",
        "text": "Page: Alberic II of Spoleto. Sentence: Alberic II (912–954) was ruler of Rome from 932 to 954, after deposing his mother Marozia and his stepfather, King Hugh of Italy.\nPage: Marozia. Sentence: Marozia, born Maria and also known as Mariuccia or Mariozza ( 890 – 937), was a Roman noblewoman who was the alleged mistress of Pope Sergius III and was given the unprecedented titles \"senatrix\" (\"senatoress\") and \"patricia\" of Rome by Pope John X.\nPage: Pope Leo VII. Sentence: Leo VII's election to the papacy was secured by Alberic II of Spoleto, the ruler of Rome at the time.\nPage: Luigi Calabresi. Sentence: Luigi Calabresi (Rome, 14 November 1937 – Milan, 17 May 1972), was a police officer and Italian State Police official in Milan, Italy.",
